      "inconsistency_hints": [
        "The trigger explicitly includes an alternative start by 'navigating to the SKU History Page from the Auction Admin Main Menu', which is a role-restricted administration workspace, but the preconditions do not establish that the Customer has access to or is already in that admin menu.",
        "The trigger claims the use case starts when the Customer selects a specific product SKU (for example, on the Product Details Page), but main flow step 1 restarts the scenario with the user entering a Product ID and clicking Go to search auction history. The PDP-selection path is not continued; the main flow assumes a different initiating action.",
        "Precondition claim 0 (and claim 1, which depends on it) places the Customer on the Product Details Page, but the trigger and main flow start from a Product ID search that opens the SKU History Page. This adds a second, unnecessary entry context alongside the Auction Admin Main Menu access in claim 3. The rule permits only one minimal entry-context claim for the admin/search workspace; the PDP availability/status claims should not be preconditions for this use case."
      ]
    }
  ],
